* TOOL_AI
* The administrator's AI choice page (S.69 step 2, plan .claude/plan-ai-step2.md and plan-fullscreen-toolkit.md A2b; owner, 23 Oct 2026: "an ai choice page. The connection
* information for each ai should be filled in except for the key and the model which the user needs to provide. There should be a checkbox for the currently selected
* provider. ... a fourth option for a user selected model where the user has to fill everything in. The same model needs to be used by all accounts. There needs to be an
* API gate for each user account").  An administrator app.
* Copyright (c) 2026, SD Core for Linux Solo.  This program is free software; you can redistribute
* it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later.
*
* START-HISTORY:
* 23 Oct 26 dm  Solo carry 15: Solo has ONE account, so the Accounts box is one row, the AI gate (set.ai gate on | off, the helper's own setting - Core's is a Linux group per
*               account, modify.account NAME ai-on), read from the helper's status instead of the register ($tk_gates is Core's and Solo has no such table).  Nothing else differs.
* 23 Oct 26 dm  (Core) New.
* 10 Nov 26 dm  SOLO CARRY (S.117): Core's shared frame, as every Core page has it: Esc and the menu bar, Ctrl-T, Ctrl-K, Ctrl-O and View > Mouse
*               ($tk_std), F6 / Shift-F6 between the boxes and the AI line ($tk_aipage, offered only refresh).  The page's own content is Solo's, unchanged.
* 11 Nov 26 dm  Carried from SD Core (S.160, 7 Nov 26, 74cf7001; the box's wording as Core has it since 8 Nov): T (and Provider > Standing text) opens the standing text -
*               the text sent first with every AI request - in a box with an editor: Save, Shipped default, Cancel; SET.AI CONTEXT keeps it.  T is not on the key row.
*               NOT carried: Core's S.209 (the page following a resize while the box is open), which needs Core's $tk_layout page; Solo's page has a fixed layout.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   TOOL.AI
*
*   For the administrator only (it is refused, before anything is read, for anyone else).  A full-screen page, in the toolkit's frame (140 columns by 43
*   lines at least), with two boxes:
*
*     Provider   Anthropic, OpenAI, DeepSeek and Custom, one to a row, with a check box on the provider in use (none marked: the AI is off), its address, its model and
*                whether its key is set.  The three named providers come with their connection details; the model and the key are the administrator's.  Custom is the fourth choice,
*                where the administrator fills in everything.  The row under the cursor is described in full below.
*     Account    The one Solo account, with the state of its ai gate (set.ai gate on | off): only while the gate is on can anything be sent to the provider.
*
*   Keys: Up and Down move, F6 or Left and Right change box, Enter selects or deselects the provider (Provider) or turns the gate on or off (Account), M the model, K the key, X clears the key,
*   C fills in Custom, D removes it, A the file of certificate authorities, L a limit, T the standing text sent with every request, F5 reads the machine again, F1 or ? or a click on a [?] explains the
*   box, Ctrl-Q leaves.
*
*   THE PAGE WRITES NOTHING ITSELF AND KNOWS NO KEY.  What it shows it reads from the AI helper (KERNEL(K$AI.STATUS): the connection details, the models, whether a key is set,
*   the gate, the limits - never a key).  Every change is a SET.AI sentence shown with its effect in a box answered
*   Run or Cancel (Cancel is what Enter chooses) and run by $tk_runx; selecting a provider, turning the gate on, a certificate file and Custom ask for a
*   name to be typed, as turning on any switch that reaches beyond SD does.  THE KEY IS NOT TYPED HERE: the page gives the terminal to SET.AI KEY, whose prompt is the AI
*   helper's own and shows nothing, then takes the screen again.  Nothing is turned on by opening the page.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
program $tool_ai
$catalog $tool_ai

$include keys.h
$include int$keys.h
$include err.h
$include sl.h
$include tk.h

   prompt ''

   allow.set = 'set.ai'                                        ;* the one command this page may run: SET.AI (through $tk_runx, which lets a word hold what SET.AI itself allows)
   okc = 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789._:/@+,-'          ;* the characters SET.AI allows in a word

   call $tk_open('tool.ai', 'admin', ctx, err)
   if err # '' then
      display err
      stop
   end
   void kernel(K$AUDIT, 'tool start app=tool.ai')

   keys = ''
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f1', 'help', 'help', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'enter', 'change', 'change', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'm', 'model', 'model', 'Provider', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'k', 'key', 'key', 'Provider', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'x', 'clear key', 'clearkey', 'Provider', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'c', 'custom', 'custom', 'Provider', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'd', 'drop custom', 'dropcustom', 'Provider', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'a', 'ca file', 'ca', 'Provider', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'l', 'limit', 'limit', 'Provider', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 't', 'standing text', 'context', '', 1)      ;* the text sent with every request, in a box (either box has it)
   keys<dcount(keys, @fm), TK.K.ROW> = 0                                   ;* bound and in the Provider menu, NOT on the key row (as in Core, whose row was full)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f5', 'refresh', 'refresh', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'ctrl-q', 'quit', 'quit', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'esc', 'menu', 'menu', '', 1)                ;* Esc opens the menu bar, as on every page
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'quit', '&File', '&Quit', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'change', '&Setting', '&Change the setting', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'model', '&Provider', '&Model', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'key', '&Provider', '&Key', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'clearkey', '&Provider', 'C&lear the key', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'custom', '&Provider', 'C&ustom provider', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'dropcustom', '&Provider', '&Drop the custom provider', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'ca', '&Provider', 'C&A file', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'limit', '&Provider', 'L&imit', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'context', '&Provider', 'S&tanding text', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'refresh', '&View', '&Refresh', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'help', '&Help', '&Help on this box', '', '')
   call $tk_std('keys', ctx, keys, '', '')                ;* Ctrl-T theme, Ctrl-K keys and their View and Help entries, as on every page
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'refresh', '', '', '', '')  ;* the AI line is offered only refresh: no change of a setting is proposed by it
   call $tk_aipage('init', ctx, keys, '', '', aout)

   provs = 'anthropic' : @fm : 'openai' : @fm : 'deepseek' : @fm : 'custom'
   lnames = 'requests-hour' : @fm : 'tokens-day' : @fm : 'timeout' : @fm : 'bytes-request' : @fm : 'bytes-reply' : @fm : 'max-tokens'
   pnames = 'Provider' : @fm : 'Account'

   VISA = 6                                                    ;* account rows on the screen
   pane = 1
   pi = 1                                                      ;* the provider row under the cursor
   ci = 1                                                      ;* the account row under the cursor
   ta = 0                                                      ;* the account rows scrolled off the top
   gen = 0
   msg = 'Enter selects the provider with the check box; M sets its model and K its key'
   done = 0

   gosub read.all
   gosub draw.all

   loop
      call $tk_menubar('draw', ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, '', '', mr)            ;* the bar first: it writes row 0 whole
      call $tk_frame(ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, msg)
      call $sl_curat(0, ctx<TK.C.YSTAT>)
      nm = ''
      screen key returning nm
      mr = ''
      ao = ''
      if nm # '' then call $tk_aipage('key', ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, nm, ao)           ;* while the AI line has the focus it takes the keys
      if ao<1> = 'replay' then nm = ao<2>                                            ;* an action the AI proposed and the person accepted
      if ao<1> # '' then msg = ao<4>
      if nm # '' and ao<1> = '' then call $tk_menubar('key', ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, nm, 0, mr)       ;* F10, Alt and a letter, and Esc: the bar
      if mr<1> # '' then nm = mr<4>
      begin case
         case ao<1> = 'taken'
            if ao<3> then
               gen += 1                                                               ;* the preview, the wait and the answer covered the page
               ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
               gosub draw.all
            end
         case nm = ''
            if status() = ER$EOF then exit
         case nm = 'guardquit'
            exit
         case nm = 'resize'
            gen += 1
            ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
            gosub draw.all
         case nm = 'mouse'
            gosub on.mouse
         case 1
            gosub on.key
      end case
      if done then exit
   repeat

   call $tk_close(ctx)
   stop

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- what the machine says

* The helper's status line (never a key), and the state of the one account's ai gate (the helper's own setting)
read.all:
   helper.ok = 0
   hj = ''
   reply = kernel(K$AI.STATUS, 0)
   if reply<1> = 'D' then
      hj = jparse(reply<2>)
      if not(status()) and hj{'t'} = 'status' then helper.ok = 1
   end
   sel = ''
   pnm = '' ; purl = '' ; pfmt = '' ; paut = '' ; pver = '' ; pmax = '' ; pmod = '' ; pkey = ''
   ca = ''
   lim = ''
   if helper.ok then
      sel = hj{'provider'}
      for i = 1 to 4
         p = provs<i>
         pnm<i> = hj{'providers/' : p : '/name'}
         purl<i> = hj{'providers/' : p : '/url'}
         pfmt<i> = hj{'providers/' : p : '/format'}
         paut<i> = hj{'providers/' : p : '/auth'}
         pver<i> = hj{'providers/' : p : '/version'}
         pmax<i> = hj{'providers/' : p : '/maxparam'}
         pmod<i> = hj{'providers/' : p : '/model'}
         pkey<i> = (if hj{'providers/' : p : '/key'} then 1 else 0)
      next i
      ca = hj{'ca-file'}
      for i = 1 to dcount(lnames, @fm)
         lim<i> = hj{'limits/' : lnames<i>}
      next i
   end
   gosub read.accounts
   return

* Solo has one account: one row, its gate read from the helper's status (when the helper cannot be reached the gate shows as off and nothing can be changed)
read.accounts:
   an = 1
   anm = 'this account' ; auser = env('USER') ; ast = 0 ; asusp = 0
   if helper.ok then
      if hj{'gate'} then ast = 1                       ;* (no short-circuit in SD BASIC: the status is only asked of when it was read)
   end
   ci = 1
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- drawing

draw.all:
   cw = ctx<TK.C.W>
   chh = ctx<TK.C.H> - 5
   screen clear at 0,1 size cw,chh
   screen box at 1,1 size 138,9 title 'AI provider'
   screen box at 1,10 size 138,13 title 'The row under the cursor'
   screen box at 1,23 size 138,10 title 'May this account use the AI?'
   screen box at 1,33 size 138,6 title 'What this means'
   gosub draw.providers
   gosub draw.detail
   gosub draw.accounts
   gosub draw.effect
   return

draw.providers:
   screen text '    ' : fmt('Provider', '14L') : fmt('Address', '56L') : fmt('Model', '28L') : 'Key' at 3,2 attr 'header' width 134
   for r = 1 to 4
      s = ''
      if helper.ok then
         nm.s = pnm<r>
         if nm.s = '' then nm.s = 'Custom'
         url.s = purl<r>
         if url.s = '' then url.s = '(not filled in)'
         if len(url.s) > 54 then url.s = url.s[1, 52] : '..'
         mod.s = pmod<r>
         if mod.s = '' then mod.s = '(not set)'
         s = '[' : (if provs<r> = sel then 'x' else ' ') : '] ' : fmt(nm.s, '14L') : fmt(url.s, '56L') : fmt(mod.s[1, 26], '28L') : (if pkey<r> then 'set' else 'not set')
      end
      screen text s at 3,2 + r attr (if r = pi then (if pane = 1 then 'highlight' else 'bold') else 'normal') width 134
   next r
   if not(helper.ok) then
      s = 'The AI helper is not running, or it is not installed: nothing here can be read or changed.'
   end else
      if sel = '' then
         s = 'The AI is OFF: no provider is selected.  Check a provider, give it a model and a key, and turn the ai gate on.'
      end else
         lpid = sel
         gosub locate.prov
         k = lpr
         s = 'In use: ' : pnm<k> : ', model ' : (if pmod<k> = '' then '(not set)' else pmod<k>) : ', key ' : (if pkey<k> then 'set' else 'not set')
         if pmod<k> = '' or not(pkey<k>) then s := '.  It cannot be used until both are set'
      end
   end
   screen text s at 3,8 attr 'bold' width 134
   call $tk_help('mark', 134, 2, 0, 0)
   return

* The row under the cursor, in full
draw.detail:
   lines = ''
   r = pi
   if not(helper.ok) then
      lines<-1> = 'No answer from the AI helper (the program sd-ai, started by your systemd user manager on the socket sd-solo-ai.sock in your runtime directory).'
   end else
      nm.s = pnm<r>
      if nm.s = '' then nm.s = 'Custom'
      if purl<r> = '' then
         lines<-1> = fmt('Name', '19L') : nm.s
         lines<-1> = fmt('Address', '19L') : '(not filled in)'
         lines<-1> = ''
         lines<-1> = "Custom is yours to fill in.  Press C and give the name, the https address, the request layout, the authentication, the version header and the name of the field that limits an answer's length."
         lines<-1> = ''
      end else
         lines<-1> = fmt('Name', '19L') : nm.s
         lines<-1> = fmt('Address', '19L') : purl<r>
         lines<-1> = fmt('Request layout', '19L') : pfmt<r> : (if pfmt<r> = 'anthropic' then '  (the Messages API)' else '  (chat completions)')
         lines<-1> = fmt('Authentication', '19L') : (if paut<r> = 'bearer' then 'Authorization: Bearer <key>' else 'x-api-key: <key>')
         lines<-1> = fmt('Version header', '19L') : (if pver<r> = '' then '(none)' else pver<r>)
         lines<-1> = fmt('Answer limit field', '19L') : pmax<r>
      end
      lines<-1> = fmt('Model', '19L') : (if pmod<r> = '' then '(not set - press M)' else pmod<r>)
      lines<-1> = fmt('Key', '19L') : (if pkey<r> then 'set (kept for the AI helper only; this page never shows it)' else 'not set - press K')
      lines<-1> = ''
      lines<-1> = 'Certificate authorities: ' : (if ca = '' then 'the system store' else ca)
      s = ''
      for i = 1 to dcount(lnames, @fm)
         s := lnames<i> : ' ' : lim<i> : (if i < dcount(lnames, @fm) then ', ' else '')
      next i
      lines<-1> = 'Limits: ' : s
   end
   gosub wrap.lines
   for r = 1 to 11
      screen text fmt(lines<r>, '134L') at 3,10 + r width 134
   next r
   return

draw.accounts:
   screen text fmt('Account', '24L') : fmt('Linux user', '24L') : 'AI gate' at 3,24 attr 'header' width 134      ;* (one row in Solo)
   if ci <= ta then ta = ci - 1
   if ci > ta + VISA then ta = ci - VISA
   if ta < 0 then ta = 0
   for r = 1 to VISA
      k = ta + r
      s = ''
      if k <= an then
         s = fmt(anm<k>, '24L') : fmt(auser<k>, '24L') : (if ast<k> = 1 then 'ON ' else 'off') : (if asusp<k> then '   (suspended)' else '')
      end
      screen text s at 3,24 + r attr (if k = ci and k <= an then (if pane = 2 then 'highlight' else 'bold') else 'normal') width 134
   next r
   if ast = 1 then
      s = 'The gate is ON: this account can send text to the provider.  Enter turns the gate off.'
   end else
      s = 'The gate is off (as delivered): nothing can be sent to the provider.  Enter turns the gate on.'
   end
   screen text s at 3,31 attr 'bold' width 134
   call $tk_help('mark', 134, 24, 0, 0)
   return

* In plain sentences
draw.effect:
   lines = ''
   lines<-1> = 'One provider and one model serve the account.  The AI is off as delivered: it needs a provider, a model, a key and the ai gate turned on.'
   lines<-1> = "The key is typed at the AI helper's own prompt and kept for the helper only; it does not pass through SD and this page never shows it.  What an account sends leaves this machine for the provider checked above, over https with the certificate checked."
   if pane = 1 then
      p = provs<pi>
      if p = sel then
         lines<-1> = 'Selected: ' : (if pnm<pi> = '' then 'Custom' else pnm<pi>) : ' is the provider in use.  Enter stops using it, which turns the AI off.'
      end else
         lines<-1> = 'Selected: ' : (if pnm<pi> = '' then 'Custom' else pnm<pi>) : ' is not in use.  Enter makes it the provider in use (you type its name to confirm).'
      end
   end else
      lines<-1> = 'Selected: ' : anm<ci> : (if ast = 1 then ' may use the AI.  Enter turns that off (at the next request).' else ' may not use the AI.  Enter turns it on (you type ai to confirm; at the next request).')
   end
   gosub wrap.lines
   for r = 1 to 4
      screen text fmt(lines<r>, '134L') at 3,33 + r width 134
   next r
   return

* A SCREEN TEXT longer than its width is cut, not wrapped
wrap.lines:
   wrapped = ''
   for wi = 1 to dcount(lines, @fm)
      if lines<wi> = '' then
         wrapped<-1> = ''
      end else
         call $tk_wrap(lines<wi>, 134, pieces)
         wrapped<-1> = pieces
      end
   next wi
   lines = wrapped
   return

* The row of the provider whose id is in lpid (1 when it is none of the four)
locate.prov:
   lpr = 1
   for lp2 = 1 to 4
      if provs<lp2> = lpid then lpr = lp2
   next lp2
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- keys and mouse

on.key:
   msg = ''
   if len(nm) = 1 and nm >= 'A' and nm <= 'Z' then nm = downcase(nm)
   begin case
      case nm = 'up'
         if pane = 1 and pi > 1 then
            pi -= 1
            gosub redraw
         end
         if pane = 2 and ci > 1 then
            ci -= 1
            gosub redraw
         end
      case nm = 'down'
         if pane = 1 and pi < 4 then
            pi += 1
            gosub redraw
         end
         if pane = 2 and ci < an then
            ci += 1
            gosub redraw
         end
      case nm = 'right' or nm = 'left'                       ;* S.176 in Core: F6 / Shift-F6 change the box, Tab no longer does (Left and Right still do)
         pane = (if pane = 1 then 2 else 1)
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'enter' or nm = ' '
         if pane = 1 then gosub select.provider else gosub toggle.gate
      case nm = 'f1' or nm = '?'
         gosub help.here
      case nm = 'f5'
         gosub read.all
         gosub draw.all
         msg = 'read the machine again'
      case nm = 'ctrl-t'                    ;* the theme, kept for the person - the same on every page ($tk_std)
         call $tk_std('theme', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
         if std.r<1> then gosub draw.all
         msg = std.r<2>
      case nm = 'act:std.mouse'             ;* View > Mouse, the same on every page ($tk_std)
         call $tk_std('mouse', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
         msg = std.r<2>
      case nm = 'ctrl-o'                    ;* the log of the commands this page ran (View > Output; $tk_std)
         call $tk_std('output', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
      case nm = 'ctrl-k'                    ;* the keys of this page, in a box
         call $tk_std('keylist', ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, std.r)
      case nm = 'f6' or nm = 'shift-f6' or nm = 'act:ai'
         call $tk_aipage('ring', ctx, keys, pane, nm : @fm : 2, ap)         ;* F6 / Shift-F6 go round the two boxes and the AI line; AI > Ask the AI goes to the line
         if ap<1> > 0 and ap<1> # pane then
            pane = ap<1>
            gosub draw.all
         end
         msg = ap<2>
      case nm = 'ctrl-q'
         done = 1
      case nm = 't'
         if helper.ok then gosub do.context else msg = sysmsg(11607)
      case nm = 'm' or nm = 'k' or nm = 'x' or nm = 'c' or nm = 'd' or nm = 'a' or nm = 'l'
         if pane # 1 then
            msg = 'Move to the Provider box (Tab) for that key'
         end else
            if not(helper.ok) then
               msg = sysmsg(11607)                                ;* The AI helper could not be reached
            end else
               begin case
                  case nm = 'm'
                     gosub do.model
                  case nm = 'k'
                     gosub do.key
                  case nm = 'x'
                     gosub do.clearkey
                  case nm = 'c'
                     gosub do.custom
                  case nm = 'd'
                     gosub do.dropcustom
                  case nm = 'a'
                     gosub do.ca
                  case nm = 'l'
                     gosub do.limit
               end case
            end
         end
   end case
   return

redraw:
   gosub draw.providers
   gosub draw.detail
   gosub draw.accounts
   gosub draw.effect
   return

on.mouse:
   screen mouse returning mev else mev = ''
   if mev = '' then return
   mr = ''
   call $tk_menubar('click', ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, mev, '', mr)                   ;* a click on the bar on row 0
   if mr<1> # '' then
      nm = mr<4>
      if nm # '' then gosub on.key
      return
   end
   call $tk_aipage('mouse', ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, mev, ap)                          ;* a click on the AI line gives it the focus
   if ap # '' then
      msg = ap
      return
   end
   call $tk_help('hit', mev, 134, 2, hit.prov)
   call $tk_help('hit', mev, 134, 24, hit.acc)
   if hit.prov or hit.acc then
      pane = (if hit.prov then 1 else 2)
      gosub redraw
      gosub help.here
      return
   end
   if mev<1> = 'press' and mev<2> = 1 then
      mx = mev<3>
      my = mev<4>
      begin case
         case mx >= 2 and mx <= 137 and my >= 3 and my <= 6
            pi = my - 2
            pane = 1
            gosub redraw
         case mx >= 2 and mx <= 137 and my >= 25 and my <= 24 + VISA
            if ta + my - 24 <= an then ci = ta + my - 24
            pane = 2
            gosub redraw
      end case
   end
   return

help.here:
   call $tk_help('box', (if pane = 1 then 'tool.ai.providers' else 'tool.ai.accounts'), hm, 0, 0)
   if hm # '' then msg = hm
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- changing something: the command, its effect, Run or Cancel, then the machine's answer

* Whether vw is a word SET.AI would take: 1 to vmax characters, all of okc
valid.word:
   vw.ok = (len(vw) >= 1 and len(vw) <= vmax)
   if vw.ok then
      if trim(convert(okc, space(len(okc)), vw)) # '' then vw.ok = 0
   end
   return

* The sentence in sent, its effect in el, the name to be typed in typed (null for Run / Cancel); every sentence is a SET.AI one (the wider word set of $tk_runx)
confirm.and.run:
   call $tk_confirm(sent, el, typed, res, cmsg)
   if res = 'run' then
      call $tk_runx(allow.set, sent, out, st, err)
      if err # '' then
         msg = err
      end else
         said = trim(change(out, @fm, ' '))
         msg = (if said # '' then said[1, 130] else 'ran, status ' : st)
      end
      gosub read.all
      gosub draw.all
   end else
      msg = cmsg
   end
   return

* Enter on a provider: check it (the one in use), or uncheck the one in use (the AI is then off)
select.provider:
   if not(helper.ok) then
      msg = sysmsg(11607)
      return
   end
   p = provs<pi>
   nm.s = pnm<pi>
   if nm.s = '' then nm.s = 'Custom'
   el = ''
   if p = sel then
      sent = 'set.ai provider none'
      typed = ''
      el<-1> = 'The AI will be off: no provider will be selected.'
      el<-1> = 'The model, the key and the ai gate stay as they are.'
   end else
      sent = 'set.ai provider ' : p
      typed = p
      el<-1> = 'From now on, while the ai gate is on, ' : nm.s : ' will be used.'
      host = field(purl<pi>, '/', 3)
      if host # '' then el<-1> = 'The text they send leaves this machine for ' : host : ' over https.'
      if pmod<pi> = '' then el<-1> = 'No model is set for it yet, so it cannot be used until you press M.'
      if not(pkey<pi>) then el<-1> = 'No key is set for it yet, so it cannot be used until you press K.'
      if p = 'custom' and purl<pi> = '' then el<-1> = 'Custom is not filled in yet: press C first (the helper refuses it until then).'
   end
   el<-1> = 'It takes effect at once.'
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

* Enter on the account: its ai gate, on or off
toggle.gate:
   if not(helper.ok) then
      msg = sysmsg(11607)
      return
   end
   on.now = (ast = 1)
   sent = 'set.ai gate ' : (if on.now then 'off' else 'on')
   el = ''
   typed = ''
   if on.now then
      el<-1> = 'This account will no longer be able to send anything to the AI.  Nothing else changes: the provider, model and key stay.'
   end else
      typed = 'ai'
      lpid = sel
      gosub locate.prov
      k = lpr
      if sel # '' then
         el<-1> = 'This account will be able to send text to ' : (if pnm<k> = '' then 'Custom' else pnm<k>) : ' with the ai verb and the programs that ask the AI.  The text leaves this machine.'
      end else
         el<-1> = 'This account will be able to use the AI as soon as you choose a provider.  What it sends leaves this machine for that provider.'
      end
      el<-1> = 'Solo runs the AI helper as you, so any program of yours can use the key the helper holds; the gate is the one switch SD keeps.'
   end
   el<-1> = 'It takes effect at the next request to the AI: the helper looks at the setting each time.'
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

* M: the model for the provider under the cursor (a dash clears it)
do.model:
   p = provs<pi>
   nm.s = pnm<pi>
   if nm.s = '' then nm.s = 'Custom'
   cur = pmod<pi>
   screen ask 'Model name for ' : nm.s : ' (a dash clears it)' width 60 value cur title 'AI model' returning mv else return
   mv = trim(mv)
   vw = mv
   vmax = 80
   gosub valid.word
   if not(vw.ok) then
      msg = 'A model name has 1 to 80 letters, digits and . _ : / @ + , - and nothing else'
      return
   end
   sent = 'set.ai model ' : p : ' ' : mv
   typed = ''
   el = ''
   if mv = '-' then
      el<-1> = 'The model for ' : nm.s : ' will be cleared.  The AI cannot be used with it until a model is set.'
   end else
      el<-1> = 'Every account that uses ' : nm.s : ' will ask model ' : mv : ' from now on.'
      el<-1> = 'The provider charges for that model; the limits shown on this page cap what accounts can send.'
   end
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

* K: the key.  The terminal is given to SET.AI KEY, whose prompt is the helper's own and shows nothing; nothing typed there reaches SD, this page or the audit trail
do.key:
   p = provs<pi>
   if index(' anthropic openai deepseek custom ', ' ' : p : ' ', 1) = 0 then return
   nm.s = pnm<pi>
   if nm.s = '' then nm.s = 'Custom'
   sent = 'set.ai key ' : p
   el = ''
   el<-1> = "The terminal is given to the AI helper's own prompt.  Type the key (nothing is shown) and press Enter.  Then you come back to this page."
   el<-1> = 'The key is kept for the helper only.  It does not pass through SD, this page or the audit trail.'
   host = field(purl<pi>, '/', 3)
   if host # '' then
      el<-1> = 'It is sent only to ' : host : ' over https, with the certificate checked.'
   end else
      el<-1> = nm.s : ' has no address yet: the key is kept, but nothing can use it until the address is filled in (press C).'
   end
   call $tk_confirm(sent, el, '', res, cmsg)
   if res # 'run' then
      msg = cmsg
      return
   end
   call $tk_close(ctx)
   execute sent
   crt
   crt sysmsg(11865) :                                         ;* Press Enter to return
   input junk
   gosub reopen
   return

* T (Core S.160; the owner, 7 Nov 26: "a standard text that will be included with every AI query describing where the default agent help text is located along any other
* information that will help the AI.  It can be accessed in a popup using a shortcut key on the AI selection pane.  It should be editable but supplied with the default
* text").  The text the helper keeps is shown in a box with an editor; Save puts it in place of the one in use, Shipped default takes the administrator's text away so that
* the default beside the helper is sent again.  The page checks the text as the helper and SET.AI will (printable ASCII and line feeds, 4000 characters) only to say so
* in the box; SET.AI CONTEXT decides, and puts it to the wall's screen.  THE SENTENCE IS RUN HERE, NOT BY $tk_runx: its one word is the text in hexadecimal, up to 8000
* characters, and $tk_runx takes 500.  The verb is fixed and the word is checked to be hexadecimal before it is run, so the sentence can hold nothing else.  The Run / Cancel
* box names the sentence with the word described, since the text itself was on the screen a moment before.
do.context:
   cx.cur = hj{'context'}
   cx.from = hj{'context-from'}
   call $sl_window(cx.scrw, cx.scrh)
   cx.w = cx.scrw - 8
   if cx.w > 120 then cx.w = 120
   cx.h = cx.scrh - 6
   if cx.h > 36 then cx.h = 36
   cx.x = int((cx.scrw - cx.w) / 2)
   cx.y = int((cx.scrh - cx.h) / 2)
   begin case
      case cx.from = 'own'
         cx.whose = "the administrator's own"
      case cx.from = 'default'
         cx.whose = 'the shipped default'
      case cx.from = 'bad'
         cx.whose = 'the kept text cannot be used, so none is sent'
      case 1
         cx.whose = 'none'
   end case
   screen form title 'Standing text sent with every AI request' at cx.x,cx.y size cx.w,cx.h returning cf
   screen label cf, 'l1', 'Sent first with every AI request; the person asking never sees it.  Now: ' : cx.whose : '.' at 2,1 width cx.w - 6
   screen label cf, 'l2', 'Plain English, 4000 characters at most.  Enter: new line.  Tab: the buttons.  Kept only after Save and Run.' at 2,2 width cx.w - 6
   screen memo cf, 'txt', convert(char(10), @fm, cx.cur) at 2,4 size cx.w - 6,cx.h - 10
   screen set cf, 'txt' wrap 1                                 ;* a long line is SHOWN on several rows; the text is not changed
   screen label cf, 'note', ' ' at 2,cx.h - 5 width cx.w - 6
   screen button cf, 'save', '&Save' at 2,cx.h - 3 default
   screen button cf, 'dflt', 'Shipped &default' at 14,cx.h - 3
   screen button cf, 'cancel', '&Cancel' at 36,cx.h - 3 cancel
   cx.act = ''
   loop
      screen wait cf returning cx.ev then                     ;* cx.ev, NOT ev: names fold case
         if cx.ev<1> = 'button' then
            begin case
               case cx.ev<2> = 'cancel'
                  cx.act = 'cancel'
               case cx.ev<2> = 'dflt'
                  cx.act = 'default'
               case cx.ev<2> = 'save'
                  screen get cf, 'txt' returning cx.new
                  cx.new = trimb(convert(@fm, char(10), cx.new))
                  loop
                  while len(cx.new) > 0 and cx.new[len(cx.new), 1] = char(10) do
                     cx.new = cx.new[1, len(cx.new) - 1]
                  repeat
                  gosub context.check
                  if cx.bad # '' then
                     screen set cf, 'note' text cx.bad
                  end else
                     cx.act = 'save'
                  end
            end case
         end
      end else
         cx.act = 'cancel'                                     ;* Esc, or an input that ended
      end
   until cx.act # ''
   repeat
   screen hide cf
   gen += 1
   ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
   gosub draw.all
   begin case
      case cx.act = 'cancel'
         msg = 'the standing text is unchanged'
         return
      case cx.act = 'default'
         if cx.from = 'default' then
            msg = 'the standing text is already the shipped default'
            return
         end
         cx.sent = 'set.ai context -'
         cx.show = cx.sent
         el = ''
         el<-1> = "The administrator's standing text is removed, and the default shipped with SD is sent with every AI request from now on."
      case 1
         if cx.new = cx.cur and cx.from # 'bad' then
            msg = 'the standing text is unchanged'
            return
         end
         cx.sent = 'set.ai context ' : oconv(cx.new, 'MX0C')
         cx.show = 'set.ai context <the text above, ' : len(cx.new) : ' characters, as hexadecimal>'
         el = ''
         el<-1> = 'Every AI request will begin with this text (' : len(cx.new) : ' characters); it is not shown in the preview.'
         el<-1> = 'A text that names SD' : "'" : 's own code or build is refused.'
   end case
   call $tk_confirm(cx.show, el, '', res, cmsg)
   if res # 'run' then
      msg = cmsg
      return
   end
   if downcase(field(cx.sent, ' ', 1)) # 'set.ai' or field(cx.sent, ' ', 2) # 'context' or dcount(cx.sent, ' ') # 3 then return
   cx.word = field(cx.sent, ' ', 3)
   if cx.word # '-' and convert('0123456789ABCDEFabcdef', '', cx.word) # '' then return       ;* the one word is hexadecimal (or -) and nothing else
   execute cx.sent trapping aborts capturing out
   said = trim(change(out, @fm, ' '))
   msg = (if said # '' then said[1, 130] else 'ran, status ' : @system.return.code)
   gosub read.all
   gosub draw.all
   return

* In: cx.new.  Out: cx.bad, null when the helper would take it, else what is wrong (said in the box)
context.check:
   cx.bad = ''
   if cx.new = '' then
      cx.bad = 'The text is empty.  To send the default again, choose Shipped default.'
      return
   end
   if len(cx.new) > 4000 then
      cx.bad = 'The text has ' : len(cx.new) : ' characters; at most 4000 are kept.'
      return
   end
   for cx.i = 1 to len(cx.new)
      cx.c = seq(cx.new[cx.i, 1])
      if cx.c # 10 and (cx.c < 32 or cx.c > 126) then
         cx.bad = 'Character ' : cx.i : ' is not plain text (only printable ASCII and new lines are kept).'
         return
      end
   next cx.i
   return

* Take the screen again after the terminal was given away; the window may have changed
reopen:
   call $tk_open('tool.ai', 'admin', ctx, err)
   if err # '' then
      display err
      done = 1
      return
   end
   gen += 1
   ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
   gosub read.all
   gosub draw.all
   msg = 'back from the key prompt: the key shows as set when it was accepted'
   return

* X: remove the key of the provider under the cursor
do.clearkey:
   p = provs<pi>
   nm.s = pnm<pi>
   if nm.s = '' then nm.s = 'Custom'
   if not(pkey<pi>) then
      msg = 'No key is set for ' : nm.s
      return
   end
   sent = 'set.ai key ' : p : ' clear'
   typed = ''
   el = ''
   el<-1> = 'The key for ' : nm.s : ' will be removed from the AI helper.  The AI cannot be used with it until a key is set again (press K).'
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

* C: the Custom row, every field the administrator's
do.custom:
   if provs<pi> # 'custom' then
      msg = 'C fills in the Custom row: move the cursor to it first'
      return
   end
   v1 = (if purl<4> = '' then '' else pnm<4>)
   v2 = purl<4>
   v3 = pfmt<4>
   v4 = paut<4>
   v5 = pver<4>
   v6 = pmax<4>
   screen ask 'Name (letters, digits and . _ : / @ + , - only)' width 40 value v1 title 'Custom AI connection  1 of 6' returning v1 else return
   screen ask 'Address: https only, no query string' width 100 value v2 title 'Custom AI connection  2 of 6' returning v2 else return
   screen ask 'Request layout: anthropic or openai' width 12 value v3 title 'Custom AI connection  3 of 6' returning v3 else return
   screen ask 'Authentication: bearer or x-api-key' width 12 value v4 title 'Custom AI connection  4 of 6' returning v4 else return
   screen ask 'Version header (empty or a dash for none)' width 24 value v5 title 'Custom AI connection  5 of 6' returning v5 else return
   screen ask 'Field that limits the length of an answer (max_tokens or max_completion_tokens)' width 30 value v6 title 'Custom AI connection  6 of 6' returning v6 else return
   v1 = trim(v1) ; v2 = trim(v2) ; v3 = downcase(trim(v3)) ; v4 = downcase(trim(v4)) ; v5 = trim(v5) ; v6 = trim(v6)
   if v5 = '' then v5 = '-'
   bad = ''
   vmax = 40 ; vw = v1 ; gosub valid.word ; if not(vw.ok) then bad = 'the name'
   vmax = 300 ; vw = v2 ; gosub valid.word ; if not(vw.ok) or v2[1, 8] # 'https://' then bad = 'the address (https://, no query string)'
   if v3 # 'anthropic' and v3 # 'openai' then bad = 'the request layout (anthropic or openai)'
   if v4 # 'bearer' and v4 # 'x-api-key' then bad = 'the authentication (bearer or x-api-key)'
   vmax = 40 ; vw = v5 ; gosub valid.word ; if not(vw.ok) then bad = 'the version header'
   vmax = 60 ; vw = v6 ; gosub valid.word ; if not(vw.ok) then bad = 'the answer length field'
   if bad # '' then
      msg = 'Not accepted: ' : bad : '.  Nothing was changed'
      gosub draw.all
      return
   end
   sent = 'set.ai custom ' : v1 : ' ' : v2 : ' ' : v3 : ' ' : v4 : ' ' : v5 : ' ' : v6
   typed = 'custom'
   el = ''
   el<-1> = 'Custom will go to ' : field(v2, '/', 3) : ' over https, with the certificate checked, and the key is sent only to that address.'
   el<-1> = 'The helper checks the address again.  It is not used until you check Custom, set a model and a key.'
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

* D: forget the Custom connection
do.dropcustom:
   if provs<pi> # 'custom' then
      msg = 'D removes the Custom row: move the cursor to it first'
      return
   end
   sent = 'set.ai custom clear'
   typed = ''
   el = ''
   el<-1> = 'The Custom connection is removed.  The helper refuses this while Custom is the provider in use.'
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

* A: the file of certificate authorities the helper trusts (instead of the system store); a dash is the system store
do.ca:
   screen ask 'File of certificate authorities for a private CA (a dash is the system store)' width 100 value ca title 'Certificate authorities' returning cv else return
   cv = trim(cv)
   vw = cv
   vmax = 300
   gosub valid.word
   if not(vw.ok) then
      msg = 'A file name here has letters, digits and . _ : / @ + , - and nothing else'
      return
   end
   sent = 'set.ai ca ' : cv
   el = ''
   if cv = '-' then
      typed = ''
      el<-1> = 'The helper will trust the system store of certificate authorities only (the delivered state).'
   end else
      typed = 'ca'
      el<-1> = 'The helper will trust ONLY the authorities in ' : cv : ', not the system store.'
      el<-1> = 'Whoever holds a key of one of those authorities can read what accounts send and the AI key.  Use a file you trust.'
   end
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

* L: one limit
do.limit:
   screen ask 'Limit (requests-hour, tokens-day, timeout, bytes-request, bytes-reply or max-tokens)' width 16 title 'AI limit' returning ln else return
   ln = downcase(trim(ln))
   locate ln in lnames<1> setting lk else
      msg = ln : ' is not one of the six limits'
      return
   end
   screen ask 'New value for ' : ln : ' (it is ' : lim<lk> : ' now; a whole number)' width 10 title 'AI limit' returning lv else return
   lv = trim(lv)
   if lv = '' or len(lv) > 9 or trim(convert('0123456789', space(10), lv)) # '' then
      msg = 'A limit is a whole number of up to 9 digits'
      return
   end
   sent = 'set.ai limit ' : ln : ' ' : lv
   typed = ''
   el = ''
   el<-1> = 'The limit ' : ln : ' will be ' : lv : ' (it is ' : lim<lk> : ' now).  The helper checks the range.'
   el<-1> = 'requests-hour and tokens-day count what each account sends; the other four cap one request.'
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

end

